\section{Conclusion}
We present \ours{}, an anatomy-anchored self-supervised pre-training framework that shifts the contrastive unit from arbitrary patches to clinically meaningful structures. \med{} bridges the natural-to-ultrasound domain gap via lightweight adapters and a learnable latent prompt engine, enabling annotation-free anatomical discovery. Inter-view anatomy-level contrast and contextual prediction jointly enforce inter-anatomy discriminability and structural coherence. Extensive evaluations confirm that \ours{} establishes a principled and clinically aligned foundation for future research in medical self-supervised learning.
