 \label{fig:SLS_Partitions}
\end{figure}
The evaluation quantifies performance using the Mean Squared Error (MSE) of the signal estimate and the cumulative output power. The BSB achieves an MSE reduction of approximately $3$ dB compared to the standard Capon beamformer. This improvement stems from the segmented approach's ability to discard covariance data from inactive interference periods, preventing null placement in directions that no longer jam the array.
To validate robustness, 100 Monte Carlo trials execute. Figure \ref{fig:SLS_MSE_MC} and Figure \ref{fig:SLS_power_MC} present the ensemble average results. The BSB consistently tracks the lower bound of the output power, adapting the integration time to match the stationarity of the environment.
