\section{Conclusion}
We introduced EchoVQA, the first large-scale VQA dataset for echocardiography, featuring 14,299 images and 74,819 QA pairs spanning diverse views, quality levels, and acquisition guidance for point-of-care settings. We further proposed a parameter-efficient method combining visual adaption prompts, text prompt learning, and test-time optimization that achieves state-of-the-art performance not only on EchoVQA but on other standard medical VQA benchmarks.
